  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "text": "Table data for all examples:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "data prop",
      "text": "You can use `data` prop to automatically generate table rows from array of React nodes.\n`data` prop accepts an object with the following properties:\n\n- `head` – an array of React nodes (`React.ReactNode[]`) to render `Table.Th` in `Table.Thead`\n- `foot` – an array of React nodes (`React.ReactNode[]`) to render `Table.Th` in `Table.Tfoot`\n- `body` - an array of arrays of React nodes (`React.ReactNode[][]`) to render `Table.Td` in `Table.Tbody`\n- `caption` – a React node to render `Table.Caption`",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sticky header",
      "text": "Set `stickyHeader` to make table header sticky. To customize top position of the header use `stickyHeaderOffset` prop:\nit is useful when you have a fixed header in your application. For example, Mantine documentation website has a fixed\nheader with 60px height:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Spacing",
      "text": "To control spacing use `horizontalSpacing` and `verticalSpacing` props. Both props support spacing from `theme.spacing` and any valid CSS value to set cell padding:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Caption and tfoot",
      "text": "Table support tfoot and caption elements. Set `captionSide` prop (top or bottom) to change caption position.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Scroll container",
      "text": "To prevent viewport overflow wrap `Table` with `Table.ScrollContainer`.\nThe component accepts `minWidth` prop which sets minimum width below which table will be scrollable.\n\nBy default, `Table.ScrollContainer` uses [ScrollArea](/core/scroll-area), you can change it\nto native scrollbars by setting `type=\"native\"`:\n\nYou can also set `maxHeight` prop on `Table.ScrollContainer` to limit table height:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vertical variant",
      "text": "Set `variant=\"vertical\"` to render table with vertical layout:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tabular numbers",
      "text": "Set `tabularNums` prop to render numbers in tabular style. It sets\n`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` which makes numbers to have equal width.\nThis is useful when you have columns with numbers and you want them to be aligned:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
